section__
  @title "Blackwater Bay Sealed Bargain beneath lion seals"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/06-endgame-siege/frame-407.jpg"

  "At Blackwater Bay, the lion-sealed truce packet arrives with blood still on the cord. Arya says the offer buys time to consolidate hospitals and reopen mills. Sandor says it buys your enemies one quiet week to rearm behind polite language. Quartermasters meanwhile report that loyalist districts are now eating two thirds rations and blaming your command for every empty bowl.

A visible legal settlement can preserve cohesion and keep crown institutions functioning into succession talks. A hidden counter-deal can fracture enemy command while pretending to negotiate in good faith, making later peace almost impossible. You can feel the act changing under your boots: this is no longer purely military theater, but pre-coronation positioning with siege weapons still firing.

The bay smells of brine, tar, and funeral smoke. Whatever promise you sign tonight becomes evidence in the history everyone survives to write."

  choice__
    @target "The Dreadfort Border Muster in crowded galleries"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Sign and announce a monitored truce framework, accepting slower gains to preserve institutional credibility."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "The Eyrie Crown Ultimatum by candle smoke"
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Feign truce compliance while funding covert defections in enemy ranks, prioritizing leverage over legitimacy."
  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "The Dreadfort Border Muster in crowded galleries"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/06-endgame-siege/frame-408.jpg"

  "The Dreadfort border galleries are packed with mercenary agents, wounded officers, and envoys counting your losses out loud. Cersei's bloc demands one final punitive campaign before settlement talks. Jaime's bloc argues that one more scorched advance will shatter bridges and depots needed to hold any crown afterward. A sellsword captain quietly offers his company's loyalty to whichever side pays first.

You stand at the final siege node before throne calculus begins. Publicly prioritizing secured corridors and demobilization can preserve survivable governance while enraging those who still expect vengeance. Quietly authorizing deniable reprisals can satisfy hardliners and drag fresh blood-feuds into the succession phase. Either choice determines the political terrain of the next act more than the battlefield terrain behind you.

Snow starts falling in wet clumps across the muster yard. The season has made its decision; now you make yours."

  choice__
    @target "The Eyrie Crown Ultimatum by candle smoke"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Order a public transition from punitive raids to secured corridors, preserving forces for succession settlement."
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "Pentos Harbor Ambush in river fog"
    @when ((secrecy + leverage) >= 5)
    @action ruthlessness = clampStat(ruthlessness + 2, 0, 30)
    @action secrecy = clampStat(secrecy + 1, 0, 30)
    @action leverage = clampStat(leverage + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Sanction covert border reprisals to break rivals before negotiations, accepting long-tail retaliation risk."
  __choice
__section
